A Customer requests a quote for a new insurance policy to understand potential costs.
A Customer submits personal information so the agent can prepare an accurate offer.
An Insurance Agent reviews the customer’s request to determine suitable coverage options.
An Insurance Agent finalizes a policy agreement so the customer can activate coverage.
An Underwriter evaluates the policy details to assess the level of risk involved.
An Underwriter adjusts the policy terms to reflect the assessed risk.
A Claims Adjuster receives a damage report from the customer to begin a claims review.
A Claims Adjuster inspects the reported damage to verify the claim.
A Claims Adjuster approves the payout so the customer can receive compensation.
An Underwriter reviews past claims to update future risk guidelines.